hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16849","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Tawus informing from Ibn Abbas from Umar, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, that he adjured people about the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning that, and Hamal ibn Malik ibn al-Nabigha came and said: I was between the houses of my two wives, and one of them struck the other with a tent pole and killed her and her fetus, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning her fetus a ghurra, a slave, and that she be killed for her. I said to Amr: Inform me no, from his father with such-and-such. He said: You have made me doubt."
